{"schema": 1, "ok": true, "kind": "physics", "tool": "", "title": "Series circuit", "order": 0, "indep": "t", "dep": "", "input_latex": "L\\,\\frac{di}{dt} + R\\,i + v_C = 0,\\qquad C\\,\\frac{dv_C}{dt} = i", "normal_latex": "L\\,\\frac{di}{dt} + R\\,i + v_C = 0,\\qquad C\\,\\frac{dv_C}{dt} = i", "rhs_expr": null, "ic": null, "summary": "Natural angular frequency = 31623 rad/s; Natural (resonance) frequency = 5.033 kHz (5033 Hz); Damping ratio = 0.1581; Ringing angular frequency = 31225 rad/s; \u2026", "other_types": [], "methods": [{"id": "solve", "name": "Step by step", "applicable": true, "reason": "Kirchhoff's voltage law: the voltages around the loop add up to the source voltage.", "steps": [{"title": "Set up the circuit equation", "text": "Kirchhoff's voltage law round the loop: the inductor's voltage \\(L\\,di/dt\\), the resistor's \\(R\\,i\\) and the capacitor's \\(v_C\\) add up to the source voltage. The current is the rate at which the capacitor charges.", "latex": ["L\\,\\frac{di}{dt} + R\\,i + v_C = 0,\\qquad C\\,\\frac{dv_C}{dt} = i"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Solve the equation", "text": "Written for the charge this is a second-order linear equation with constant coefficients, the same as a mass on a spring (L plays the mass, R the damping, 1/C the spring). Its characteristic equation \\(L r^2 + R r + 1/C = 0\\) decides whether the circuit rings; the source adds a particular solution, and the constants come from the initial voltage and current.", "latex": ["L\\,q'' + R\\,q' + \\frac{q}{C} = V(t),\\qquad q = C\\,v_C", "\\zeta < 1:\\ q_h = e^{-\\zeta\\omega_0 t}(A\\cos\\omega_d t + B\\sin\\omega_d t)", "\\zeta = 1:\\ q_h = (A + B t)\\,e^{-\\omega_0 t},\\qquad \\zeta > 1:\\ q_h = A e^{r_1 t} + B e^{r_2 t}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "List the known values", "text": "Everything is converted to SI units before it goes into the equations.", "latex": [], "substeps": [], "table": {"headers": ["\\text{quantity}", "\\text{symbol}", "\\text{given}", "\\text{SI}"], "rows": [["\\text{Resistance}", "R", "10\\ \\mathrm{\\Omega}", "10\\ \\mathrm{\\Omega}"], ["\\text{Inductance}", "L", "1\\ \\mathrm{mH}", "0.001\\ \\mathrm{H}"], ["\\text{Capacitance}", "C", "1\\ \\mathrm{\\mu F}", "1 \\times 10^{-6}\\ \\mathrm{F}"], ["\\text{Initial capacitor voltage}", "V_0", "10\\ \\mathrm{V}", "10\\ \\mathrm{V}"], ["\\text{Initial current}", "I_0", "0\\ \\mathrm{A}", "0\\ \\mathrm{A}"], ["\\text{Time}", "t", "0.2\\ \\mathrm{ms}", "0.0002\\ \\mathrm{s}"]]}}, {"title": "Find the natural angular frequency", "text": "The natural frequency of an inductor and a capacitor exchanging energy. With \\(L = 1\\ \\mathrm{mH}\\), \\(C = 1\\ \\mathrm{\\mu F}\\).", "latex": ["\\omega_0 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{L C}}", "\\omega_0 = 31623\\ \\mathrm{rad/s}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the natural (resonance) frequency", "text": "Frequency in cycles per second. With \\(\\omega_0 = 31623\\ \\mathrm{rad/s}\\).", "latex": ["f_0 = \\frac{\\omega_0}{2\\pi}", "f_0 = 5.033\\ \\mathrm{kHz}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the damping ratio", "text": "The damping ratio compares the resistance with the critical value. With \\(L = 1\\ \\mathrm{mH}\\), \\(C = 1\\ \\mathrm{\\mu F}\\), \\(R = 10\\ \\mathrm{\\Omega}\\).", "latex": ["\\zeta = \\frac{R}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{C}{L}}", "\\zeta = 0.1581"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the ringing angular frequency", "text": "Resistance lowers the ringing frequency (underdamped case only). With \\(\\omega_0 = 31623\\ \\mathrm{rad/s}\\), \\(\\zeta = 0.1581\\).", "latex": ["\\omega_d = \\omega_0\\sqrt{1 - \\zeta^2}", "\\omega_d = 31225\\ \\mathrm{rad/s}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the quality factor", "text": "The quality factor measures how sharp the resonance is. With \\(\\zeta = 0.1581\\).", "latex": ["Q = \\frac{1}{2\\zeta}", "Q = 3.162"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the capacitor voltage at that time", "text": "The capacitor voltage at time t from the solution of the circuit equation. With \\(t = 0.2\\ \\mathrm{ms}\\), \\(L = 1\\ \\mathrm{mH}\\), \\(C = 1\\ \\mathrm{\\mu F}\\), \\(V_0 = 10\\ \\mathrm{V}\\), \\(I_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{A}\\), \\(R = 10\\ \\mathrm{\\Omega}\\). This relation is solved for \\(v_C\\) numerically (bisection).", "latex": ["v_C = v_C(t)", "v_C = 3.654\\ \\mathrm{V}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the charge at that time", "text": "Charge on a capacitor. With \\(C = 1\\ \\mathrm{\\mu F}\\), \\(v_C = 3.654\\ \\mathrm{V}\\).", "latex": ["q = C\\,v_C", "q = 3.654 \\times 10^{-6}\\ \\mathrm{C}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the energy in the capacitor at that time", "text": "Energy stored in a capacitor. With \\(C = 1\\ \\mathrm{\\mu F}\\), \\(v_C = 3.654\\ \\mathrm{V}\\).", "latex": ["E_C = \\tfrac12 C v_C^2", "E_C = 6.674 \\times 10^{-6}\\ \\mathrm{J}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the current at that time", "text": "The current at time t from the solution of the circuit equation. With \\(t = 0.2\\ \\mathrm{ms}\\), \\(L = 1\\ \\mathrm{mH}\\), \\(C = 1\\ \\mathrm{\\mu F}\\), \\(V_0 = 10\\ \\mathrm{V}\\), \\(I_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{A}\\), \\(R = 10\\ \\mathrm{\\Omega}\\). This relation is solved for \\(i\\) numerically (bisection).", "latex": ["i = i(t)", "i = 4.498\\ \\mathrm{mA}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the energy in the inductor at that time", "text": "Energy stored in an inductor. With \\(L = 1\\ \\mathrm{mH}\\), \\(i = 4.498\\ \\mathrm{mA}\\).", "latex": ["E_L = \\tfrac12 L i^2", "E_L = 1.012 \\times 10^{-8}\\ \\mathrm{J}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the inductor voltage at that time", "text": "The inductor takes whatever voltage the other parts of the loop do not. With \\(t = 0.2\\ \\mathrm{ms}\\), \\(i = 4.498\\ \\mathrm{mA}\\), \\(v_C = 3.654\\ \\mathrm{V}\\), \\(R = 10\\ \\mathrm{\\Omega}\\).", "latex": ["v_L = V(t) - R\\,i - v_C", "v_L = -3.699\\ \\mathrm{V}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Summary", "text": "", "latex": [], "substeps": [], "table": {"headers": ["\\text{quantity}", "\\text{symbol}", "\\text{value}", ""], 